# COMPLETE

This document checks four deliverables: today's DIALS detection limit, the cause of its misses,
a tested improvement and reproducible findings. It also checks agreement with the paper and the
remaining limits. Measurements are from the results files of commit `{{ n.commit }}`
(`python -m cf.report && python -m cf.render`; `bash reproduce.sh` regenerates every number from the
raw data). Each line gives the measurement and the reference it is checked against; details in
`FINDINGS.md` (claims and evidence, including the held-out judgements and limits).

## 1. Today's DIALS reproduces the published separation

- 36 cryo crystals, `xia2.multiplex` with every default: {{ n.fidelity.multiplex_cryo_full.n_clusters }} clusters
  ({{ n.fidelity.multiplex_cryo_full.clusters|clusters }}), {{ n.fidelity.multiplex_cryo_full.n_outliers }}
  outliers, {{ n.fidelity.multiplex_cryo_full.dims }} dimensions, resolution filter {{ n.fidelity.multiplex_cryo_full.resolution_filter }} A;
  the paper: three pure clusters, no outliers, three dimensions, 1.26 A. **Reproduced.**
- Cut to 1.0 and 0.8 degrees per crystal: {{ n.fidelity.multiplex_cryo_10_images.n_clusters }} and
  {{ n.fidelity.multiplex_cryo_8_images.n_clusters }} species-pure clusters with {{ n.fidelity.multiplex_cryo_10_images.n_outliers }}
  and {{ n.fidelity.multiplex_cryo_8_images.n_outliers }} outlier; the paper: separated down to 0.8 degrees. Reproduced, one
  porcine crystal an outlier at 0.8 degrees.
- The paper's own cosym coordinates shipped with DIALS: cryo labels reproduced exactly; the 215
  room-temperature data sets give 83, 82, 28 and 22 outliers against the published 83, 85, 28 and 19
  (three data sets become outliers under today's defaults, which changed after the paper).

