## 3. Deliverable 2: the cause, by evidence

Replaying today's DIALS from every trial's own correlation matrix with one stage changed: lowering the
OPTICS minimum-samples floor (5) to 2 makes it report minorities of 2-4 at full data
({{ n[C ~ '|cause'].floor2.detection.values()|list|length and '' }}cryo k=2-4 at 10 degrees:
{% set d = n[C ~ '|cause'] %}{{ (d.default.detection.get('10|2', [0,0])[0] + d.default.detection.get('10|3', [0,0])[0] + d.default.detection.get('10|4', [0,0])[0]) }} found with the floor,
{{ (d.floor2.detection.get('10|2', [0,0])[0] + d.floor2.detection.get('10|3', [0,0])[0] + d.floor2.detection.get('10|4', [0,0])[0]) }}
without it, of {{ (d.default.detection.get('10|2', [0,0])[1] + d.default.detection.get('10|3', [0,0])[1] + d.default.detection.get('10|4', [0,0])[1]) }}),
and groups in single-population data ({{ d.floor2.false_groups.values()|map('first')|sum }} of
{{ d.floor2.false_groups.values()|map('last')|sum }} trials against {{ d.default.false_groups.values()|map('first')|sum }}); changing the number of
dimensions, the min_samples search or the scaling of the coordinates changes nothing. The minority is
already separated in the coordinates OPTICS receives (cryo, full data: median silhouette of the true
split {{ '%.2f'|format(d.separability['10|2'].silhouette_median) }}-{{ '%.2f'|format(d.separability['10|4'].silhouette_median) }},
every minority crystal's nearest neighbour a minority crystal in {{ '%.0f'|format(100 * d.separability['10|3'].nn_pure) }}-{{ '%.0f'|format(100 * d.separability['10|4'].nn_pure) }}% of draws).
The cause is OPTICS's minimum cluster size: density clustering has no measure of how far a group stands
out of the noise, so its floor is what keeps noise and structure inside one species from being reported,
and it loses every group below it.{% set dr = n.get(R ~ '|cause') %}{% if dr and dr.get('floor2') %} Room temperature, the same (60 degrees, `FINDINGS.md` F3):
{{ dr.default.detection.get('60|2', [0,0])[0] + dr.default.detection.get('60|3', [0,0])[0] + dr.default.detection.get('60|4', [0,0])[0] }} of
{{ dr.default.detection.get('60|2', [0,0])[1] + dr.default.detection.get('60|3', [0,0])[1] + dr.default.detection.get('60|4', [0,0])[1] }} minorities of 2-4 found with the floor,
{{ dr.floor2.detection.get('60|2', [0,0])[0] + dr.floor2.detection.get('60|3', [0,0])[0] + dr.floor2.detection.get('60|4', [0,0])[0] }} without it, and groups in
{{ dr.floor2.false_groups.values()|map('first')|sum }} of {{ dr.floor2.false_groups.values()|map('last')|sum }} single-population trials against {{ dr.default.false_groups.values()|map('first')|sum }}.{% endif %}

